            "body": "| Feature | Ideal Solution | Positive (+ve) Deviation | Negative (−ve) Deviation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Intermolecular Forces** | A–B ≈ A–A, B–B | **A–B WEAKER** than A–A, B–B (molecules escape easily!) | **A–B STRONGER** than A–A, B–B (molecules held tightly!) |\n| **Vapour Pressure** | P = p_A° x_A + p_B° x_B | **P > Raoult's value** | **P < Raoult's value** |\n| **ΔH_mix** | **0** | **> 0 (Endothermic — cools!)** | **< 0 (Exothermic — warms!)** |\n| **ΔV_mix** | **0** | **> 0 (Expands!)** | **< 0 (Contracts!)** |\n| **Azeotrope Type** | None (separable!) | **Minimum-boiling azeotrope** | **Maximum-boiling azeotrope** |\n| **Classic Examples** | n-Hexane + n-Heptane; Benzene + Toluene; Bromoethane + Chloroethane | **Ethanol + Acetone**; **Ethanol + Water (95%!)**; CS₂ + Acetone | **Chloroform + Acetone** (new H-bond!); **HNO₃ + Water (68%)**; Phenol + Aniline |\n\n*(Kyun Chloroform + Acetone mein −ve deviation hota hai? Kyunki CHCl₃ ka H aur Acetone ka O milkar naya **Hydrogen Bond** bana lete hain — jisse molecules ka bhaap banna mushkil ho jaata hai aur P ghat jaata hai!)*",
