            "bodyHinglish": "Tej ek organometallic chemistry seminar mein tha jahan professor ne 3 isoelectronic carbonyls dikhaye: [V(CO)₆]⁻, [Cr(CO)₆], aur [Mn(CO)₆]⁺. Teeno octahedral hain aur teeno mein exact 18 valence electrons hain! Professor ne poocha: \"In teeno mein sabse kamzor (sabse lamba) C–O bond kis mein hoga?\" Tej ne turant back-bonding ka logic lagaya: \"V⁻ par negative charge hai → sabse zyada electron density → sabse zyada π* back-donation → **[V(CO)₆]⁻ mein sabse kamzor C–O bond**!\""
