            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Uma ek chemical manufacturing video dekh rahi thi jahan ethanol se chloroethane banane ke teen tareeke dikhaye gaye: PCl₅ ke saath, PCl₃ ke saath, aur **SOCl₂ (thionyl chloride)** ke saath. Factory engineer ne kaha, \"Hum hamesha **SOCl₂** choose karte hain!\" Uma ne socha, \"Kyun?\" Engineer ne dikhaya: SOCl₂ ke saath jo by-products bante hain — SO₂ aur HCl — woh dono **gases** hain jo upar ud jati hain, aur neeche bilkul **100% pure chloroethane** bachta hai!\n\n> **Safety Note:** Thionyl chloride (SOCl₂), phosphorus halides, bromine (Br₂), aur diazonium salts corrosive/toxic hote hain; yeh reactions sirf fume-hood industrial/research setups aur theory mein padhi jati hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Uma ek chemical manufacturing video dekh rahi thi jahan ethanol se chloroethane banane ke teen tareeke dikhaye gaye: PCl₅ ke saath, PCl₃ ke saath, aur **SOCl₂ (thionyl chloride)** ke saath. Factory engineer ne kaha, \"Hum hamesha **SOCl₂** choose karte hain!\" Uma ne socha, \"Kyun?\" Engineer ne dikhaya: SOCl₂ ke saath jo by-products bante hain — SO₂ aur HCl — woh dono **gases** hain jo upar ud jati hain, aur neeche bilkul **100% pure chloroethane** bachta hai!\n\n> **Safety Note:** Thionyl chloride (SOCl₂), phosphorus halides, bromine (Br₂), aur diazonium salts corrosive/toxic hote hain; yeh reactions sirf fume-hood industrial/research setups aur theory mein padhi jati hain."
