            "bodyHinglish": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Nucleophilic Substitution (SN)** | Woh reaction jismein ek stronger nucleophile (Nu⁻) haloalkane se halide leaving group (X⁻) ko replace kar deta hai |\n| **SN2 Mechanism** | Bimolecular (2nd order), single-step backside attack with **Walden inversion** (Rate = k[R–X][Nu⁻]) |\n| **SN1 Mechanism** | Unimolecular (1st order), two-step mechanism via a planar **carbocation** intermediate with **racemisation** (Rate = k[R–X]) |\n| **Ambident Nucleophile** | Woh nucleophile jiske paas do alag nucleophilic attacking atoms hon (jaise CN⁻: C ya N; NO₂⁻: O ya N) |\n| **Zaitsev (Saytzeff) Rule** | Dehydrohalogenation (β-elimination) mein woh alkene **major product** hota hai jismein C=C double bond par **sabse zyada alkyl groups** (zyada substituted alkene) jude hon |\n| **Grignard Reagent (R–Mg–X)** | Organometallic reagent jo R–X + Mg (dry ether) se banta hai; carbon par δ⁻ charge (strong base & nucleophile!) |"
