            "headingHinglish": "1. Physical Properties of Haloalkanes & Haloarenes",
            "body": "1. **Boiling Points (BP):**\n   - For the same alkyl group: **R–I > R–Br > R–Cl > R–F** (halogen ka mass aur size badhne se van der Waals forces badhti hain).\n   - For isomeric haloalkanes: **Branching badhne par BP GHAT-TA hai!** Kyunki branching se molecule spherical ho jata hai → surface area kam → weaker van der Waals forces!\n     Example: **1-Bromobutane (375 K) > 2-Bromobutane (364 K) > 2-Bromo-2-methylpropane (346 K)**.\n2. **Melting Points of Dichlorobenzenes (Symmetry Effect!):**\n   - **para-Dichlorobenzene** ka melting point ortho aur meta isomers se **bahut zyada** (323 K vs 256 K, 249 K) hota hai! Kyunki para isomer **symmetrical** hai aur crystal lattice mein tightly pack ho jata hai!\n3. **Solubility:** Polar hone ke bawajood haloalkanes **paani mein almost insoluble** hote hain! Kyunki yeh paani ke strong intermolecular H-bonds ko todne ke liye zaroori energy release nahi kar paate (organic solvents mein soluble hain).",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. **Boiling Points (BP):**\n   - For the same alkyl group: **R–I > R–Br > R–Cl > R–F** (halogen ka mass aur size badhne se van der Waals forces badhti hain).\n   - For isomeric haloalkanes: **Branching badhne par BP GHAT-TA hai!** Kyunki branching se molecule spherical ho jata hai → surface area kam → weaker van der Waals forces!\n     Example: **1-Bromobutane (375 K) > 2-Bromobutane (364 K) > 2-Bromo-2-methylpropane (346 K)**.\n2. **Melting Points of Dichlorobenzenes (Symmetry Effect!):**\n   - **para-Dichlorobenzene** ka melting point ortho aur meta isomers se **bahut zyada** (323 K vs 256 K, 249 K) hota hai! Kyunki para isomer **symmetrical** hai aur crystal lattice mein tightly pack ho jata hai!\n3. **Solubility:** Polar hone ke bawajood haloalkanes **paani mein almost insoluble** hote hain! Kyunki yeh paani ke strong intermolecular H-bonds ko todne ke liye zaroori energy release nahi kar paate (organic solvents mein soluble hain)."
