            "headingHinglish": "1. Stereochemistry: Chirality & SN1/SN2 Outcomes",
            "body": "- **Condition for optical activity:** Molecule **chiral** (asymmetric — no plane of symmetry, non-superimposable mirror image) hona chahiye.\n- Example: **2-Bromobutane** (CH₃–CH(Br)–CH₂CH₃) mein C2 par 4 alag groups (–H, –Br, –CH₃, –C₂H₅) hain → **chiral (optically active)**!\n- **Propan-2-ol** (CH₃–CH(OH)–CH₃) mein C2 par do same –CH₃ groups hain → **achiral (optically inactive)**!\n- **SN2 on optically active halide:** Backside attack causes **100% inversion** (e.g., (−)-2-bromooctane + OH⁻ → (+)-octan-2-ol).\n- **SN1 on optically active halide:** Planar sp² carbocation allows equal front & back attack → **racemisation** (± mixture, optically inactive!).",
