            "body": "- **Shifting halogen position:** 1-halo → (alc. KOH) → alkene → (HBr) → 2-halo; reverse uses **HBr + peroxide**!\n- **Distinguishing R–Cl / ArCH₂Cl vs Ar–Cl:** Warm aq. KOH + dil. HNO₃ + AgNO₃ → white AgCl ppt ONLY for alkyl/benzylic/allylic chlorides, NOT aryl/vinylic chlorides!\n- **Ring activation trick:** Nitrate chlorobenzene FIRST, then hydrolyse with NaOH at 443 K (much easier than Dow's 623 K!).",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Shifting halogen position:** 1-halo → (alc. KOH) → alkene → (HBr) → 2-halo; reverse uses **HBr + peroxide**!\n- **Distinguishing R–Cl / ArCH₂Cl vs Ar–Cl:** Warm aq. KOH + dil. HNO₃ + AgNO₃ → white AgCl ppt ONLY for alkyl/benzylic/allylic chlorides, NOT aryl/vinylic chlorides!\n- **Ring activation trick:** Nitrate chlorobenzene FIRST, then hydrolyse with NaOH at 443 K (much easier than Dow's 623 K!)."
