            "bodyHinglish": "Akshara ek organic mechanism tutorial mein ek surprising result dekh rahi thi: optically active (S)-2-butanol ko jab pure **SOCl₂** ke saath react karwaya gaya, toh **(S)-2-chlorobutane (Retention!)** mila — par jaise hi usmein thoda **pyridine** dala gaya, product **(R)-2-chlorobutane (Inversion!)** ban gaya! Mentor ne samjhaya: \"Bina pyridine ke reaction **SNi (Internal Nucleophilic Substitution)** se jati hai, aur pyridine dalte hi Cl⁻ free hokar **SN2 backside attack** kar deta hai!\""
