            "headingHinglish": "2. Preparation of Phenols (4 Methods!)",
            "body": "1. **From Haloarenes (Dow's Process):**\n   C₆H₅–Cl + NaOH —(623 K, 300 atm)→ C₆H₅–ONa —(HCl)→ **C₆H₅–OH**.\n2. **From Benzenesulphonic Acid:**\n   Benzene + Oleum (H₂S₂O₇) → C₆H₅–SO₃H —(1. molten NaOH, 2. H⁺)→ **C₆H₅–OH**.\n3. **From Diazonium Salts (Lab Method):**\n   Aniline —(NaNO₂ + HCl, 0–5°C)→ C₆H₅–N₂⁺Cl⁻ —(warm H₂O)→ **C₆H₅–OH** + N₂↑ + HCl.\n4. **From Cumene (Commercial / Industrial Method — MOST IMPORTANT!):**\n   - Step 1 (Air oxidation): C₆H₅–CH(CH₃)₂ (Cumene) + O₂ → **C₆H₅–C(CH₃)₂–O–O–H** (Cumene hydroperoxide)\n   - Step 2 (Dilute acid H⁺ / H₂O): Cumene hydroperoxide → **C₆H₅–OH (Phenol)** + **CH₃–CO–CH₃ (Acetone)**!",
