            "body": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Esterification** | Alcohol/Phenol + Carboxylic acid (ya acid anhydride/chloride) → Ester + H₂O (aspirin synthesis isi ka example hai) |\n| **PCC (Pyridinium Chlorochromate)** | Mild oxidising agent jo **1° alcohol ko sirf aldehyde tak** rok deta hai (acid tak nahi le jata!) |\n| **Kolbe's Reaction** | Sodium phenoxide + CO₂ (400 K, 4–7 atm), phir H⁺ → **Salicylic acid (2-hydroxybenzoic acid)** |\n| **Reimer–Tiemann Reaction** | Phenol + CHCl₃ + aq. NaOH (340 K), phir H⁺ → **Salicylaldehyde (2-hydroxybenzaldehyde)** (intermediate: dichlorocarbene :CCl₂) |\n| **Benzoquinone** | Phenol ke Na₂Cr₂O₇ + H₂SO₄ oxidation se bana conjugated diketone |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Esterification** | Alcohol/Phenol + Carboxylic acid (ya acid anhydride/chloride) → Ester + H₂O (aspirin synthesis isi ka example hai) |\n| **PCC (Pyridinium Chlorochromate)** | Mild oxidising agent jo **1° alcohol ko sirf aldehyde tak** rok deta hai (acid tak nahi le jata!) |\n| **Kolbe's Reaction** | Sodium phenoxide + CO₂ (400 K, 4–7 atm), phir H⁺ → **Salicylic acid (2-hydroxybenzoic acid)** |\n| **Reimer–Tiemann Reaction** | Phenol + CHCl₃ + aq. NaOH (340 K), phir H⁺ → **Salicylaldehyde (2-hydroxybenzaldehyde)** (intermediate: dichlorocarbene :CCl₂) |\n| **Benzoquinone** | Phenol ke Na₂Cr₂O₇ + H₂SO₄ oxidation se bana conjugated diketone |"
