            "body": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Carbonyl Group (>C=O)** | Carbon–oxygen double bond jo aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, esters, amides sab mein maujood hota hai |\n| **Aldehyde (R–CHO)** | Woh carbonyl compound jismein C=O carbon kam se kam ek **hydrogen atom** se juda ho (chain ke end par hota hai) |\n| **Ketone (R–CO–R')** | Woh carbonyl compound jismein C=O carbon **do carbon atoms (alkyl/aryl)** ke beech juda ho |\n| **Carboxylic Acid (R–COOH)** | Woh compound jismein carbonyl group (>C=O) aur hydroxyl group (–OH) ek hi carbon par jude hon (carboxyl group) |\n| **α-Carbon & α-Hydrogen** | Carbonyl carbon (>C=O) ke **theek bagal wala** sp³ carbon atom aur us par jude hydrogens |",
