            "body": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **α-Amino Acid** | Woh organic compound jismein –NH₂ aur –COOH dono ek hi α-carbon par jude hon: R–CH(NH₂)–COOH |\n| **Essential Amino Acids** | Woh 10 amino acids jo hamara sharir khud nahi bana sakta aur humein **diet (khaane)** se lene padte hain (jaise Valine, Leucine, Lysine) |\n| **Zwitterion** | Amino acid ka neutral dipolar ion form (**⁺H₃N–CH(R)–COO⁻**) jismein + aur − dono charges ek saath maujood hon |\n| **Peptide Linkage (–CO–NH–)** | Ek amino acid ke –COOH aur doosre ke –NH₂ ke beech paani (H₂O) nikalne se bana amide bond |\n| **Fibrous vs Globular Proteins** | **Fibrous** = lambe thread-like, water-insoluble (keratin, myosin); **Globular** = spherical folded, water-soluble (insulin, albumin) |\n| **Denaturation** | Temperature ya pH badalne se protein ke **H-bonds tootna**, jisse uski **2°, 3°, aur 4° structures** aur biological activity nasht ho jati hai (par **1° structure intact** rehti hai!) |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Term | Hinglish Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **α-Amino Acid** | Woh organic compound jismein –NH₂ aur –COOH dono ek hi α-carbon par jude hon: R–CH(NH₂)–COOH |\n| **Essential Amino Acids** | Woh 10 amino acids jo hamara sharir khud nahi bana sakta aur humein **diet (khaane)** se lene padte hain (jaise Valine, Leucine, Lysine) |\n| **Zwitterion** | Amino acid ka neutral dipolar ion form (**⁺H₃N–CH(R)–COO⁻**) jismein + aur − dono charges ek saath maujood hon |\n| **Peptide Linkage (–CO–NH–)** | Ek amino acid ke –COOH aur doosre ke –NH₂ ke beech paani (H₂O) nikalne se bana amide bond |\n| **Fibrous vs Globular Proteins** | **Fibrous** = lambe thread-like, water-insoluble (keratin, myosin); **Globular** = spherical folded, water-soluble (insulin, albumin) |\n| **Denaturation** | Temperature ya pH badalne se protein ke **H-bonds tootna**, jisse uski **2°, 3°, aur 4° structures** aur biological activity nasht ho jati hai (par **1° structure intact** rehti hai!) |"
